= Constant-product market maker — Simple =

A constant-product market maker is an AMM built around the relation x × y = k for two reserves. Trading changes the reserve balance and therefore the price. Larger trades relative to the pool move the price more.

'''Important boundary:''' constant-product market maker ≠ every AMM.

